From 848131280482af56f4711da77e6f58ac55f539ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:58:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 59/76] perf(trace): parallel copy-cycle counting and fill

Phase 1 now runs over fixed-size row chunks of all blocks (the arithmetic
block dominates, so a per-block split left cores idle) and records each wire
cell's real variable index in a flat array in (block, row, wire) order.
Counting and filling the CSR copy cycles are split by variable ranges: each
thread scans all cells in order and handles only its own variables, so each
cycle's nodes keep the same order as the serial pass. Replaces the per-block
(variable, node) staging vectors (12 bytes per cell) with 4 bytes per cell.
